      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add IPv6 fallback for status menu IP",
        "body": "Closes #4\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds IPv6 fallback support for the status menu IP row.\r\n\r\nThe status menu still prefers IPv4 when a usable IPv4 address is available, preserving the existing behavior. When no IPv4 address is found, it now falls back to a usable IPv6 address so IPv6-only and NAT64-style environments do not show `IP -` with copying disabled.\r\n\r\nThe IPv6 fallback filters out unspecified, loopback, multicast, link-local, and unique-local addresses, then keeps the existing interface ranking so `en*` interfaces are preferred over tunnel/VPN interfaces.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- `swift build`\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n\r\nDirect selector proof:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPROOF mixed-prefers-ipv4 address=192.0.2.10 interface=utun9\r\nPROOF ipv6-only-fallback address=2001:4860:4860::8888 interface=en1\r\nPROOF link-local-only address=nil\r\nPROOF ipv6-ranking address=2001:4860:4860::8888 interface=en0\r\n```",
        "branch": "fix/issue-4-ipv6-status-menu",
